# WHAT ENTERS (committed to `src/` on feat/shape-constraint-solver in this same lane):
#   - parser (`ast.tks`, `parse_decl.tks`): two new `@ConstraintExpr()` members — `ConstraintForm`
#     (the form words `class`/`struct`/`service`, the last optionally carrying a `ServiceLifetime`) and
#     `ConstraintNotNull` (the `notnull` modifier). The constraint grammar reads the form keywords, a
#     contextual lifetime word after `service`, and a contextual `notnull`; it REJECTS `notnull` on
#     either side of a `|` (a modifier is never a shape-alternative).
#   - checker (`monomorph.tks`, `resolve.tks`, `merge.tks`): `constraint_form_satisfied` resolves a form
#     word against the type-argument's declaration (reusing `is_class_name`/`is_struct_name`, adding
#     `is_service_name`/`service_lifetime_of`/`lifetime_eq`), and a named lifetime must MATCH — the §9.2b
#     honest-lifetime ruling, where a wrong-lifetime transport fails at the instantiation point instead of
#     being coerced to singleton. `constraint_notnull_satisfied` rejects a null/nullable type-argument.
#     A constraint atom naming no TypeDecl now falls back to `builtin_type`, so a CONCRETE type term
#     (`str`, `i64`, …) forces identity. Form/notnull terms name no interface and contribute no callable
#     surface. The pre-existing ConstraintAnd/ConstraintOr tree supplies the disjunction of conjunctions.
#   - emit (`tkb_write.tks`, `tkb_frame.tks`, `tkb_read.tks`): the two new members ride the `.tkb` codec
#     as constraint tags 4 (NotNull) and 5 (Form: interned form word + has_lifetime u8 + lifetime u8).
#   Carried forward: the completed §9.D sweep and every rung under it (CR1/CR2/CR3, the union-of-unions
#   nested group-option, the Error/Null marker dedup, §14 A0-A4 / B1-B5, §14 Form 2 parametric
#   type-macros, §9.D capabilities (a)/(b)/(c)).
